            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This is *somewhat* expected because `|` is built-in modifier with the [following behavior](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/88f18a7d018d8bb4d32f6be4c712134a10e826d3/doc/mini-align.txt#L346-L357). What happens here is:\r\n- Both lines are split by `|`. The whitespace text before the first `|` in first line is treated as a text part.\r\n- All parts are then [trimmed from left and right whitespace](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/88f18a7d018d8bb4d32f6be4c712134a10e826d3/doc/mini-align.txt#L294-L303) but in a way to preserve indentation (which is the leading whitespace in the first line).\r\n- All parts are justified appropriately, which makes second line the same indentation as the first.\r\n- All parts are merged with separator padded with a single space from left and right. This adds the single space to the left.\r\n\r\nI'll take a look if there is a reasonable workaround for not adding merge space to the left (to more strongly preserve indentation), but no promises.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">This is <em>somewhat</em> expected because <code class=\"notranslate\">|</code> is built-in modifier with the <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/88f18a7d018d8bb4d32f6be4c712134a10e826d3/doc/mini-align.txt#L346-L357\">following behavior</a>. What happens here is:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Both lines are split by <code class=\"notranslate\">|</code>. The whitespace text before the first <code class=\"notranslate\">|</code> in first line is treated as a text part.</li>\n<li>All parts are then <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/88f18a7d018d8bb4d32f6be4c712134a10e826d3/doc/mini-align.txt#L294-L303\">trimmed from left and right whitespace</a> but in a way to preserve indentation (which is the leading whitespace in the first line).</li>\n<li>All parts are justified appropriately, which makes second line the same indentation as the first.</li>\n<li>All parts are merged with separator padded with a single space from left and right. This adds the single space to the left.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'll take a look if there is a reasonable workaround for not adding merge space to the left (to more strongly preserve indentation), but no promises.</p>",
            "bodyText": "This is somewhat expected because | is built-in modifier with the following behavior. What happens here is:\n\nBoth lines are split by |. The whitespace text before the first | in first line is treated as a text part.\nAll parts are then trimmed from left and right whitespace but in a way to preserve indentation (which is the leading whitespace in the first line).\nAll parts are justified appropriately, which makes second line the same indentation as the first.\nAll parts are merged with separator padded with a single space from left and right. This adds the single space to the left.\n\nI'll take a look if there is a reasonable workaround for not adding merge space to the left (to more strongly preserve indentation), but no promises.",
